UID:0f867f0c-5422-4d44-93b8-d7faaae7019b@spacex-launch-alerts
DTSTAMP:20261118T092537Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261118T092537Z
SEQUENCE:217157137
SUMMARY:✅ Starship · Starlink Group 31-2 (Starship Flight 15)
DTSTART:20261113T224736Z
DTEND:20261114T000236Z
LOCATION:Orbital Launch Pad 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Status: Launch Successful\nWindow: Fri\, 13 Nov 2026 22:45:00 U
 TC – Sat\, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 UTC\nOrbit: Low Earth Orbit\nPad: Orbita
 l Launch Pad 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA\n\n▶ Watch live: https://www
 .youtube.com/watch?v=dl4O6RqbvOs\n\n15th test flight of the two-stage Star
 ship launch vehicle and 4th flight of Starship V3. Second Starship flight 
 to deploy satellites (a group of Starlink satellites known as Starlink Gro
 up 31-2) into stable Low Earth Orbit and first ever to attempt returning t
 he Starship 2nd stage back to the launch site.\n\nThe ship is expected to 
 fly at an altitude approximately 275 km above Earth and complete approxima
 tely 14 orbits around the planet for more than 22 hours\, with the ship ex
 pected to attempt returning back to Starbase\, Texas on its launch pad by 
 pad arms catching.\n\nThe booster’s primary test objective on Flight 15 
 will be executing a successful launch\, ascent\, stage separation\, boostb
 ack burn\, and landing by pad arms catching. This will also be the 1st Sta
 rship V3 booster to attempt returning to its launch site.\n\nStarship will
  deliver 26 Starlink V3 satellites to orbit for the second time\, which ai
 m to greatly expand the network's capacity and user speeds. Each Starlink 
 V3 satellite will add 1 Tbps of capacity to the constellation. 3 of the sa
 tellites have been modified with a suite of cameras to scan Starship’s h
 eatshield and transmit imagery down to operators.\n\nCountdown & updates: 
 https://benjaminowens612.github.io/spacex-launch-alerts/#0f867f0c-5422-4d4
 4-93b8-d7faaae7019b
URL:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dl4O6RqbvOs
CATEGORIES:starlink,starship
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
